    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and the 16 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't run a coverage check, so the 90% gate is untested.\n\nThe function validates everything first: region, category, `qty` (a `bool` is rejected), price, discount and credit. It then computes each line net with the discount and the extra multiplied 5% bulk discount. Each line net and each line tax is rounded to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, and the totals are sums of the rounded line values. Credit is applied to the gross, and `tax_by_rate` is keyed by integer rate, including a 0 rate when a line has one.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- the empty list;\n- the tax rates in both regions;\n- the bulk-plus-discount case (85.5%);\n- per-line rounding;\n- credit smaller and larger than the gross;\n- each error case;\n- the discount limits of 0 and 100.",
